lens:
CRO (Baymard/CXL school, D2C jewellery India), round 6. This lens measures add-to-cart and checkout rate for a shopper who lands from an Instagram ad at 360x640 in the in-app browser. It covers first-screen decision content, the buy path (Add to bag, Buy now, the sticky bar, the moment after adding), the 20% drop from add to checkout, the Buy 2/3/4 ladder and AOV, COD against prepaid, ad message match, friction and distraction, and the test plan.

G3 passes. fold.png, added.png, fold-ad.png, screens_1-5.jpg and measure.json (06:59:17-21) are newer than prototype.html (06:58:55, md5 74dcaeee...). My fresh render of an untouched copy is md5-identical to fold.png (d4ae18d6...). The first screen is unchanged since round 4. fold-ad.png equals fold.png by design.

Evidence is in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/aaed4e78-f5ea-57f6-bb8a-ea8f2c0ecee0/scratchpad/cro_r6:
- probe.js and probe.json: the buy path, the bag with one and two pieces, Buy now, landings, a card-mode sweep over 92 scroll positions, and first adds at 320x568, 390x664 and 412x732;
- probe2.js and probe2.json: the bag total against the foot, at 1-4 pieces on five viewports;
- probe3.js: the in-bag ring add;
- probe4.js and probe4.json: the two-line card in rupees;
- screenshots: fold_now.png, bag1.png, bag2.png, bag_*.png, bag_after_drawer_add.png, buynow.png, card_ring.png, ring_only.png, add0_*.png.
Fixes 2 and 3 were checked on copies, never on the prototype:
- var/prototype.html (md5 2cba01e3...) with var_probe2.json and var_bag_*.png;
- var2/prototype.html (md5 91104563...) with var2_add_160.png and var2_add_1200.png.
I also read the repo at origin/main bd412960: supabase/functions/meta-capi/index.ts and guard.ts, src/lib/pixel.ts, visitorId.ts, fastrr.ts, shopify.ts and payment.ts, and index.html.

All four of my round-5 fixes landed:
- the slim card keeps the ring at scrollY 90-120 (85-253), and on the first add at 320x568 (85-291);
- the bag's policy opens in place, remedy first, and Secure checkout stays at 580-628;
- the dock sits over the macro photo, keys its set link on #set-h, and the tick holds 1.5 s;
- build note 8 exists.
No-card positions on the 50px grid fell from 40/60 to 34/60.

Two things are wrong, and one of them is mine.
(1) Build note 8 carries my round-5 text verbatim, and it is wrong about the codebase. meta-capi never receives Purchase: guard.ts RELAYED_EVENTS excludes it, and index.ts L77 says 'never Purchase'. So the fallback 'orders are joined on the Purchase event' cannot run. Nothing named in the note can produce its own decision metrics (visitors who added / PDP visitors, by arm): Meta's dataset stats split only by event, device and host (research_data section 0), and meta-capi stores nothing. The SHA-256 step is also asynchronous, so it cannot decide the layout before React renders, and naira_vid is already a random UUID.
(2) Round 5's short policy line under Secure checkout (trust 8) grew the bag foot by 25px. In the two-piece bag at 360x640, the case this page is built to produce, the Cormorant total now sits at 459-496, and the foot starts at 486, so the total is cut by 10px. It is cut the same way straight after the bag's own '+ ADD' (450-496 against 486). In rounds 4 and 5 the foot started at 511.

score_now is the weighted mean of the same 14 criteria as rounds 3-5: 676.4 / 76 = 8.90, reported as 8.9. The gains in C5, C7 and C20 are offset by C21. The critique is also saved to /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/aaed4e78-f5ea-57f6-bb8a-ea8f2c0ecee0/scratchpad/pdp10/rounds/r6_cro.json.

